---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Cookies & storage"
  description="My website remembers only your local theme and motion choices. I use no analytics, advertising cookies or embedded social feeds."
>
  <section class="wrap prose-page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR BROWSER, YOUR CHOICE</p>
      <h1>
        A few preferences.
        <br />
        No tracking scripts.
      </h1>
      <p>
        Updated <time datetime="2026-10-28">28 October 2026</time>.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What this website remembers</h2>
      <p>
        The website code does not set cookies. It uses two local-storage entries
        for choices you make:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Theme:</strong> light or dark appearance, stored as{' '}
          <code>wizardloop-theme</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Motion:</strong> whether you paused animation, stored as{' '}
          <code>wizardloop-motion</code>. Your system's reduced-motion
          preference is also respected.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Local storage is different from a cookie, but both store information in
        your browser. These settings remain until you change them or clear this
        website's data. They are not used to identify visitors or build a
        marketing profile. If storage is unavailable, the site remains usable
        and your choices may apply only to the current visit.
      </p>
      <h2>No embedded services</h2>
      <p>
        The site has no advertising, analytics, social widgets, CAPTCHA or
        embedded Telegram feed. It does not need a banner asking permission to
        load those features. Links to Telegram and GitHub take you to their
        websites only when you choose to follow them; their own storage and
        privacy rules then apply.
      </p>
      <h2>Change or clear your choices</h2>
      <p>
        Use the theme and motion buttons in the header. To reset all saved
        choices, clear the data for <strong>wizardloop.com</strong> in your
        browser's site settings. An older version's Telegram preference, if
        present, is no longer read or used and is removed when you clear the
        site's data.
      </p>
      <p>
        These statements describe the website code, not independent hosting
        security logs or data stored by websites you visit through links. Read
        the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> or{' '}
        <a href="/feedback/">contact me</a> if you have a question.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
